# Read from the CONTEXT ROOT, which is this directory — the build needs the workspace's manifests,
# so it cannot be scoped to apps/portal/, and an ignore file placed beside the Dockerfile would be
# consulted by nothing.
#
# A .env reaching the build context is a secret leak that no test of the built image can see: the
# runtime stage copies only dist/, so anything that leaks in is invisible downstream and permanent
# upstream. The build stage asserts these are absent for that reason.

.git
.github
.claude
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
infra
lambdas
docs
**/dist
**/coverage
htmlcov
**/__pycache__
